we move on. Anything tempting that's not in the PRD goes in FUTURE.md, not in
the app. Real empty and error states on every screen, and when something fails
the copy names the real cause.20:["$","div","12",{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-dim","children":"Copy and paste"}],["$","$L17",null,{"text":"$2e"}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"rounded-xl bg-[#0a1020] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[#e4e9f5] overflow-x-auto","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"$2f"}]}]]}]
21:["$","p","13",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"The non-goals section is the one people delete. Leave it in. It's the only thing standing between you and a settings screen with fourteen toggles nobody asked for."}]
22:["$","h2","14",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"Prompt 4: Make it not look vibecoded"}]
23:["$","p","15",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"This is the step everyone skips, and it's why their app screams that AI made it. A design system before any screen gets touched, then the three moments that actually sell: first open, the core loop, and the paywall."}]
24:["$","div","16",{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-dim","children":"Copy and paste"}],["$","$L17",null,{"text":"You're a senior product designer doing a full pass on my app. First, build the\ndesign system. Don't touch a screen until it exists: a real palette (near-black\nbase, ONE accent color, semantic colors used only for meaning), one type family\nwith a proper scale, spacing on a 4pt grid, one corner radius language. Write\nthem down as tokens.\n\nBanned: default blue, system-font energy, gradients on everything,\npurple-to-pink hero sections, emoji as icons, five different button styles.\n\nThen redesign every screen against those tokens, and obsess over the three\nmoments that sell the app: first open, the core loop, and the paywall. The\npaywall should feel like a VIP invite, not a ransom note, with price and renewal\nterms stated plainly. That honesty converts AND keeps you out of trouble.\n\nDeliver clickable HTML mockups of the 5 core screens so I can walk through them\nbefore we touch the real code."}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"rounded-xl bg-[#0a1020] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[#e4e9f5] overflow-x-auto","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"You're a senior product designer doing a full pass on my app. First, build the\ndesign system. Don't touch a screen until it exists: a real palette (near-black\nbase, ONE accent color, semantic colors used only for meaning), one type family\nwith a proper scale, spacing on a 4pt grid, one corner radius language. Write\nthem down as tokens.\n\nBanned: default blue, system-font energy, gradients on everything,\npurple-to-pink hero sections, emoji as icons, five different button styles.\n\nThen redesign every screen against those tokens, and obsess over the three\nmoments that sell the app: first open, the core loop, and the paywall. The\npaywall should feel like a VIP invite, not a ransom note, with price and renewal\nterms stated plainly. That honesty converts AND keeps you out of trouble.\n\nDeliver clickable HTML mockups of the 5 core screens so I can walk through them\nbefore we touch the real code."}]}]]}]
25:["$","p","17",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Mockups before code, every time. Redesigning an HTML file costs you ten minutes. Redesigning a built app costs you a weekend and half your motivation."}]
26:["$","h2","18",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"Prompt 5: The $10k math and the weekly loop"}]
27:["$","p","19",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"Ten grand a month is just an equation. Make Claude solve it backwards so you know exactly which number you're attacking on any given Monday."}]
28:["$","div","20",{"className":"mt-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 flex items-center justify-between gap-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-[12px] text-ink-dim","children":"Copy and paste"}],["$","$L17",null,{"text":"My app charges [$X/mo, $Y/yr]. Work the equation backwards from $10,000/mo:\nhow many paying subscribers is that, and, using realistic freemium conversion\nrates rather than fantasy ones, how many installs does that require, and how\nmuch traffic does THAT require. Show the full funnel with the numbers at each\nstep, then tell me which single conversion step is most worth attacking first.\n\nThen build the growth system:\n1. ASO: 30 keyword targets ranked by (volume / competition), plus title and\n   subtitle variants to test.\n2. Screenshot copy: 5 captions that sell the outcome, not the features.\n3. 10 short-form hooks for TikTok and Reels: build-in-public angle,\n   before/after angle, and \"I found a gap\" angle.\n4. The weekly loop, as an actual checklist. Every Monday: read the week's new\n   reviews, ship the #1 complaint, post 3 videos, check the funnel number we're\n   attacking. Repeat until the equation balances."}]]}],["$","pre",null,{"className":"rounded-xl bg-[#0a1020] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[#e4e9f5] overflow-x-auto","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"My app charges [$X/mo, $Y/yr]. Work the equation backwards from $10,000/mo:\nhow many paying subscribers is that, and, using realistic freemium conversion\nrates rather than fantasy ones, how many installs does that require, and how\nmuch traffic does THAT require. Show the full funnel with the numbers at each\nstep, then tell me which single conversion step is most worth attacking first.\n\nThen build the growth system:\n1. ASO: 30 keyword targets ranked by (volume / competition), plus title and\n   subtitle variants to test.\n2. Screenshot copy: 5 captions that sell the outcome, not the features.\n3. 10 short-form hooks for TikTok and Reels: build-in-public angle,\n   before/after angle, and \"I found a gap\" angle.\n4. The weekly loop, as an actual checklist. Every Monday: read the week's new\n   reviews, ship the #1 complaint, post 3 videos, check the funnel number we're\n   attacking. Repeat until the equation balances."}]}]]}]
29:["$","p","21",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"That last checklist is the whole business. Read the reviews, ship the top complaint, post the videos, watch the one number."}]
2a:["$","h2","22",{"className":"mt-12 t-h3 text-ink","children":"Why the order matters"}]
2b:["$","p","23",{"className":"mt-5 text-lg leading-[1.75] text-ink","children":"The prompts aren't the magic. The magic is that each one produces a document the next one runs on. Gap into teardown, teardown into PRD, PRD into design, design into funnel. Run them out of order and you get five disconnected chat sessions. Run them in order and you get an operating system."}]
